    id: "s-gen-part2-a-bicycle-motorcycle-car-trip-you-would-like-to-go-aug2026",
    title: "Describe a bicycle/motorcycle/car trip you would like to go",
    part: "part2",
    band: "8.0",
    questions: [
      "Cue card: Describe a bicycle/motorcycle/car trip you would like to go",
    ],
    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "If I'm honest, this question is a bit tricky for me, because I don't really dream about bicycle, motorcycle, or car trips the way a lot of people seem to. I get motion sickness fairly easily, so long rides, whether by car, coach, or motorbike, have never been something I look forward to — if anything, I try to avoid them whenever I can.\n\nSo rather than pretending I'm secretly plotting some long road trip, I'll describe the one kind of \"trip\" I could actually imagine enjoying: a short Grab bike hop across town, from my apartment over to a little bookstore-café that opened in District 1 a few weeks ago. It's only about fifteen or twenty minutes away, but I've been curious about the place since I saw it on someone's Instagram story.\n\nWhat makes a Grab bike bearable for me, compared to sitting in a car, is that I'm upright and moving with the bike rather than being jostled around inside a sealed box, which is usually what triggers the nausea. It's short enough that I wouldn't need to worry about feeling sick halfway through, and I could just hop off, browse some books, have a coffee, then book another bike home whenever I'm ready.\n\nI know it probably sounds unambitious compared to someone describing a scenic coastal motorbike journey, but that's genuinely closer to my comfort zone. If a trip has to happen at all, I'd rather it be short, local, and easy to escape from than long and adventurous, something I'd secretly be dreading the whole time. Honestly, given a completely free choice, I might just admit I'd rather stay home that day.",
