    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "A change I made fairly recently is switching almost all my grocery shopping from the wet market near my building to delivery apps instead. It might sound like a minor lifestyle tweak, but it's actually changed my daily routine quite a bit.\n\nFor years I did what most people around here do — popped down to the market most mornings, picked fish or vegetables by eye, chatted with the same few sellers. It worked fine until I started job-hunting seriously, with video interviews and paperwork often scheduled early, sometimes as early as eight. Getting up, going to the market, cooking, and still being ready and presentable for a call became a tight squeeze most days.\n\nSo a few months ago I just tried ordering a full week's groceries through an app instead, mostly out of curiosity rather than a firm plan. It went smoother than expected — prices weren't wildly different, delivery usually arrived within the hour, and I could schedule orders the night before instead of thinking about it each morning. I kept doing it, and eventually the market trips became occasional rather than daily.\n\nThe result has been more free time and less stress in the mornings, which I now spend preparing for interviews or just calming my nerves properly instead of rushing. I do miss the small talk with market sellers sometimes, and I'm slightly pickier now about which app vendors actually pack fresh produce properly. Overall though, it's one of those quiet changes that didn't feel big in the moment but has genuinely reshaped how my average day runs lately.",
