    questions: [
      "Cue card: Describe a child who loves drawing/painting",
    ],
    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "I'd like to talk about my niece, Mi, who's seven and, according to basically everyone in the family, was drawing before she could properly write her own name. She's my older sister's daughter, so I see her fairly often at family gatherings, and there's rarely a visit where she isn't holding a marker of some sort.\n\nWhat made me really notice it was one weekend when I was babysitting her while my sister ran errands. Within maybe ten minutes of arriving at my apartment, she'd already found a stack of scrap paper on my desk, the kind I use for lesson notes, and started drawing without even asking. I expected simple stick figures, but instead she drew this oddly detailed scene of our whole extended family standing outside grandma's house, everyone labelled with slightly misspelled names and, strangely, our dog wearing sunglasses for no reason she could explain.\n\nWhat struck me most wasn't really the skill itself, since obviously a seven-year-old's drawing isn't technically impressive, but her total focus. She tuned out the cartoon playing on the TV, ignored me asking twice if she wanted a snack, and just kept adding tiny details — a cloud here, a flower there — completely absorbed in her own little world.\n\nMy sister says Mi now fills an entire sketchbook every month, and teachers at her kindergarten have started saving her drawings instead of sending them home. I don't know if she'll stick with art as she gets older, but for now that stubborn, undistracted concentration is something I wish I still had when trying to focus on anything for more than five minutes.",
