    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The city I'd like to talk about is Đà Nẵng, a coastal city in central Vietnam that I visited with a group of former coworkers last year for a long weekend, back when we were all still at the same office.\n\nI'll admit I almost turned the trip down at first, mainly because I'm not someone who jumps at travel opportunities — I get motion sickness fairly easily, and the idea of a long overland journey never appeals to me. But since Đà Nẵng has its own international airport, we simply flew there from Ho Chi Minh City in about an hour, which made the whole thing far more manageable than I expected, without the usual nausea I associate with longer road trips.\n\nOnce we landed, we skipped the taxi queue and booked Grab bikes straight into the city instead, weaving through traffic to our hotel near the beach in about fifteen minutes. Over the weekend, we walked along the beachfront in the late afternoon, ate incredibly fresh seafood at a plastic-table restaurant a local recommended, and crossed the Dragon Bridge on foot just to see it up close, mostly for the photos rather than any deep fascination with bridges.\n\nWhat made it enjoyable wasn't spectacular scenery exactly, though the beach was genuinely lovely — it was how manageable the whole trip felt from start to finish. Flying in kept the travel time short, Grab bikes made getting around the city painless, and by the time we flew home on Sunday evening, I'd honestly enjoyed myself far more than my usual travel reluctance would have predicted.",
