    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The long-term goal I've held onto for a couple of years now is opening my own small bookstore-café somewhere in Ho Chi Minh City — nothing huge, just a cosy shop with decent coffee and shelves I've actually curated myself.\n\nThe idea started almost by accident. After I left my office job, I suddenly had free weekends for the first time in years, and I began wandering into small independent bookshops and cafés around the city, partly out of boredom and partly out of genuine curiosity about how they were run. The more places I visited, the more I pictured myself behind that counter instead of just sitting at a table with my drink.\n\nIt's difficult mainly because of money and confidence. Renting even a modest space isn't cheap, and I have zero experience actually running a business — I don't know suppliers, pricing, or how to manage staff if I ever needed any. For now, I'm saving gradually from freelance work I've picked up while job-hunting, and I keep a notebook of ideas: shelf layout, which genres to stock, even a rough name I keep changing my mind about.\n\nI haven't achieved it yet, so I can't pretend to know how satisfying it'll actually feel. But working toward it already changes how I spend my days — instead of scrolling job listings all afternoon, I'll research supplier prices or read about small business regulations. Whether it takes two years or five, I'd rather build it slowly and properly than rush in underprepared. It still feels achievable, which is honestly the main thing keeping me motivated through this in-between stretch of my life.",
