    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "My idea of a perfect future job is running a small café, or maybe a bookstore — I honestly go back and forth between the two, depending on my mood that week. It's not really about turning a big profit; it's more about having a small place that genuinely feels like mine, somewhere I could spend my days doing something I actually enjoy instead of clocking in somewhere else.\n\nI used to work a fairly typical office job — sales admin, fixed hours, a commute through traffic every single day. It paid reasonably well, but I never felt any real ownership over what I did there; I was just one small part of a system that would keep running whether I stayed or left. Since leaving that job a while back, I've had time to actually picture what I'd want instead, and this quiet little shop idea keeps coming back stronger than anything else.\n\nIn my head, it's nothing fancy: a handful of tables, decent coffee, shelves of secondhand books people can borrow or buy, maybe a reading corner near a window. I wouldn't need it to expand into a chain or make me rich; I'd just want enough regulars to cover the rent and let me keep the lights on comfortably.\n\nWhat makes it \"perfect\" to me isn't status or income, but control — deciding the playlist, the menu, which books go on the shelf, without answering to anyone above me. I'm not there yet; right now I'm still saving and researching rental prices around the city. But it's the version of \"job\" that actually excites me, rather than one I'd just tolerate for a paycheque.",
