    band: "8.0",
    questions: [
      "Cue card: Describe a person who likes to look after the natural world",
    ],
    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "I'd like to talk about Ông Ba, an elderly man who lives near the small canal not far from my apartment. He's retired now, in his seventies, and pretty much every morning he's out there doing something related to the trees and the water around our block.\n\nI first noticed him properly during a walk one evening when I saw him sweeping fallen leaves and, more surprisingly, fishing plastic bags and bottles out of the canal with a long stick he clearly made himself. I asked why he bothered, since it's not really \"his job,\" and he just shrugged and said the smell gets unbearable in the rainy season if nobody deals with it, so he might as well be the one doing it.\n\nBeyond the canal, he also looks after an old tree right at the corner of the alley, one that's probably older than most of the residents combined. He waters it, ties up branches that droop too low over the path, and gets genuinely annoyed at anyone who parks a motorbike carelessly against the trunk. He also puts out small bowls of water for birds and stray cats during the hottest months, which sounds minor but I've never seen anyone else in the neighbourhood bother.\n\nI wouldn't describe him as an environmentalist in any formal sense — he'd probably laugh at that word. He's just someone who treats the immediate space he lives in, the tree, the canal, the strays, as things worth maintaining rather than someone else's problem. Compared to how easily the rest of us walk past the same mess every day, his quiet, consistent effort genuinely stands out.",
