    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The piece of local news I want to describe is the opening of Ho Chi Minh City's first metro line, which practically everyone around me was talking about for weeks, both online and in person.\n\nI remember scrolling through my phone and seeing the announcement everywhere — friends posting videos from inside the carriages, neighbours discussing it in the building group chat, even my own mother bringing it up twice during ordinary dinner conversations. After years of construction, traffic diversions, and honestly a fair amount of public scepticism about whether it would ever actually open, seeing trains running felt like a genuinely big deal for the city.\n\nWhat made it especially interesting wasn't just the technology itself but people's reactions. Some were thrilled about finally having an alternative to sitting in traffic on a motorbike every day; others worried aloud about ticket prices, station access, or whether it would actually reduce congestion on the roads above. My mother, who rarely comments on city infrastructure, mentioned it twice at dinner, mostly amazed that trains were running underground in a city she's lived in her whole life.\n\nI haven't ridden it myself yet, but I've watched plenty of clips and read local coverage almost daily during the first couple of weeks. It's the kind of story that goes beyond just being \"news\" — it touches something people feel personally, since traffic is such a constant headache here. Whether it truly changes daily commuting long-term is still an open question, but for now it's given the whole city something hopeful and slightly novel to talk about.",
