    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The piece of technology I'd really like to own is an e-reader, something like a Kindle or one of the equivalent Vietnamese-made devices with a paper-like screen. I don't have one yet, mainly because even the basic models are still fairly pricey for someone currently between jobs, but it's been sitting on my wish list for a long time.\n\nThe main reason is simply how much I read. I've always loved books, and right now, with more free time than I've had in years, I read even more than usual — partly for enjoyment, partly to distract myself from constantly checking job listings. My shelves at home are already overflowing, and buying physical copies of everything I want is starting to feel both expensive and impractical in a one-bedroom apartment with limited space.\n\nWith an e-reader, I could carry an entire library around without adding a single kilogram of clutter, adjust the text size for late-night reading without straining my eyes, and borrow ebooks from library apps instead of always buying new copies. It would also charge only once every couple of weeks, unlike my phone, which I already stare at too much while browsing job apps.\n\nBeyond the practical side, I imagine it becoming something calming rather than just useful — a screen that doesn't buzz with notifications or job alerts, just quiet pages. So it's partly practical and partly a small comfort purchase, which is probably why I keep adding one to my cart and then closing the tab before actually buying it.",
