    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The place I'd like to recommend is Đà Lạt, a small city up in the Central Highlands that I visited with two close friends about a year ago, and that I still bring up whenever people ask for weekend-trip ideas.\n\nSince I'm honestly not much of a traveller — motion sickness makes long journeys pretty unpleasant — I made sure this trip involved as little discomfort as possible. Instead of the overnight sleeper coach everyone else seems to take, we flew from Tân Sơn Nhất straight into Liên Khương Airport, which took less than an hour and spared me the queasy road version entirely. I'll admit the short flight still gave me a slightly uneasy stomach during takeoff, but nothing compared to what a six-hour coach ride would have done.\n\nFrom the airport, we each booked a Grab bike into the city centre rather than negotiating with taxi drivers, which felt both cheaper and, oddly, steadier for my stomach than sitting in a car winding down mountain roads. Once we'd arrived, it was completely worth the effort. The air felt cooler and cleaner than Ho Chi Minh City, we wandered through flower gardens, drank surprisingly good local coffee at quiet little cafés, and spent one evening just sitting by Xuân Hương Lake doing basically nothing, which suited me perfectly.\n\nWhat makes me recommend it isn't adventure — it's that Đà Lạt feels calm without being boring, and reachable without a punishing journey, as long as you fly in and hop on a Grab bike rather than committing to hours on a coach.",
