    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The place I'd like to visit in my free time is a rooftop bookstore-café that opened somewhere in District 3 last year, which a couple of friends have mentioned enthusiastically but which I still haven't actually gotten around to visiting myself.\n\nFrom what I've seen on social media, it's a converted old apartment building with narrow, slightly creaky stairs leading up to a rooftop space filled with secondhand books, small potted plants, and mismatched furniture that somehow works together. Apparently you can sit up there for hours with a single drink, reading or just people-watching over the rooftops of the district, without anyone rushing you to order more.\n\nI keep meaning to go, mostly because it sounds like exactly the kind of low-effort outing that suits me — no long journey required, no need to plan an entire day, just a short ride across the city and then hours of doing absolutely nothing productive. As someone who spends most weekdays glued to a laptop screen scrolling job listings, the idea of somewhere quiet with actual physical books instead of another screen feels oddly appealing right now.\n\nI haven't gone yet mainly because weekends keep getting swallowed by errands and interview prep, which is honestly a fairly familiar excuse these days. But I've saved the location, and I keep telling myself I'll finally go once things settle down, maybe treating myself as a small reward once I land something.\n\nIf it's even half as charming as it looks online, I imagine it becoming a regular spot rather than a one-off visit, precisely because it doesn't ask much of me beyond showing up and sitting still for a while.",
