    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "If I'm being completely honest, I don't actually have a real short-term job lined up abroad, and I don't have much of a genuine plan to work overseas at all right now. I'm currently between jobs after leaving an office position I'd been doing for a few years, and most of my energy goes into figuring out what to do next here in Ho Chi Minh City, not overseas.\n\nBut if a cue card forces me to imagine one, I'd probably pick something low-pressure and slightly amusing rather than anything career-boosting: working as a sales clerk in a small bookstore somewhere abroad, or, failing that, doing food delivery for a few weeks. Neither is a genuine ambition — they're just the two ideas that come to mind because they actually suit me. I've always loved reading, so restocking shelves and quietly organising a shop full of books sounds oddly relaxing rather than stressful, even in a language I'm not fully comfortable in.\n\nThe honest complication is that I'm not really a traveller. I get seriously carsick — say xe, as we call it — so long flights and unfamiliar transport already sound exhausting before I even consider job duties. If I ever did this, it would need an easy flight into somewhere with Grab-bike-style transport already running, so I could skip taxis entirely, and I'd probably spend half my wages calling home out of homesickness.\n\nSo realistically, this stays a \"what if\" rather than a plan. Between jobs, I'm more focused on sorting out something local and steady, maybe eventually saving toward the small bookstore I keep imagining for myself one day.",
