    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "I'd like to talk about a day out with my best friend a few months ago, right after we'd both had a really stressful week at work. Neither of us had much money to spare, so we decided to keep things simple and stay somewhere close to home instead of planning anything elaborate.\n\nWe started the morning with iced coffee from a small quán cóc near my apartment — the kind of plastic-stool café that costs less than fifty thousand đồng for two drinks. Then we just walked along the Saigon riverside walkway for almost two hours, chatting about everything and nothing, from work drama to childhood memories. It sounds like a small thing, but honestly, walking without any fixed plan felt surprisingly refreshing after weeks of rushing between lessons and deadlines.\n\nFor lunch, we grabbed bánh mì from a street cart and ate it sitting on a bench, watching people jog and kids play badminton nearby. In the afternoon, we dropped into a bookshop just to browse, not to buy, and ended the day with grilled corn from a night vendor before heading home. The entire day probably cost less than a proper restaurant meal, yet it turned out to be one of the most relaxing outings I'd had in a while.\n\nWhat made it special wasn't spending money on anything fancy — it was slowing down and actually being present with someone I care about. Ever since then, I've realised a good day out doesn't need a big budget; it just needs decent company and a bit of unhurried time, which I honestly enjoy far more than a heavily-planned trip somewhere far away.",
