    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The tall building I want to talk about is Landmark 81, currently the tallest building in Vietnam, sitting right along the Saigon River not far from where I live. I can actually see its top floors from my apartment window on clear evenings, lit up like a giant glowing pillar over the city.\n\nI went up to the Skyview observation deck once, about two years ago, when a friend visiting from another province insisted we do the typical tourist thing. The elevator ride alone was disorienting — it shoots up so fast that my ears popped and my stomach did a small flip, which, given how easily I get queasy on anything that moves too fast, wasn't exactly comfortable. Once we reached the top, though, the view genuinely impressed me: the whole city spread out in a hazy grid of rooftops, the river cutting through it, motorbikes reduced to tiny moving dots far below.\n\nI mostly like the building, though not unconditionally. Landmark 81 has become a proper symbol of the city's modern skyline, something people point to in photos to show how much HCMC has grown. At the same time, part of me finds it a little disconnected from the older, messier charm of the city — the narrow alleys, street food stalls, and low rooftops that actually feel like home to me.\n\nSo my honest answer is a mixed one: impressive to look at, worth visiting once for the view, but not somewhere I'd want to go regularly. I'm happier admiring it from a safe distance, ideally from ground level, with both feet firmly on solid pavement.",
