    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "I want to describe an evening I got stuck in traffic for almost two hours on my motorbike near Nguyễn Hữu Cảnh street, which is honestly one of the most notorious flooding spots in Ho Chi Minh City.\n\nIt had been raining heavily for most of the afternoon, and by the time I finished a late lesson and headed home around six, the road was already half-flooded and packed with motorbikes and buses barely inching forward. What normally takes me about twenty minutes turned into a complete standstill — engines were cutting out in the deeper puddles, a bus had stalled sideways, and everyone was just trying to squeeze past without falling into a pothole hidden under the water.\n\nAt one point I genuinely couldn't move at all for what felt like forty minutes, wedged between a delivery driver balancing boxes and a bus blasting its horn for no real reason, since nobody could go anywhere anyway. My legs got soaked, my phone battery was dying, and I remember messaging a student to reschedule because there was clearly no way I'd make it home in time to teach.\n\nWhat got me through it was honestly just other people's dark humour — strangers laughing about the situation, someone joking that the street should just be renamed a river during rainy season. By the time I finally reached my building, completely drenched, I was too tired to even be properly angry. It was a reminder of how unpredictable commuting is here, and also why I've never minded that I don't own a car — on a night like that, it wouldn't have helped at all.",
