    answers: [],
    modelMonologue: "The program I've been watching regularly lately is \"2 Ngày 1 Đêm,\" the Vietnamese version of that Korean travel-variety format where a group of celebrities gets sent to different provinces and has to complete slightly ridiculous challenges to earn food or avoid sleeping outside.\n\nI got into it almost by accident — a clip showed up on my phone one evening while I was scrolling instead of sleeping, and within a week I'd gone through an embarrassing number of episodes. There's something almost funny about my own attachment to this particular show, because as most people who know me will tell you, I'm not really a traveller myself; long trips and buses tend to leave me feeling seasick, so I usually just stay home given the choice.\n\nThat's actually part of the appeal, though. Watching the cast get dropped into unfamiliar mountain towns, argue over silly games, and occasionally fail spectacularly at simple tasks lets me enjoy the scenery and the chaos completely secondhand, from my own sofa, without any of the motion sickness or exhaustion I'd get if I actually went along. The editing is fast-paced, the games are genuinely entertaining rather than scripted-feeling, and the friendships between the regular cast members feel real after enough episodes.\n\nI usually watch an episode late at night as a way to unwind after a fairly uneventful day of job-hunting and errands, and it's become a small, reliable ritual — probably my favourite kind of \"travelling,\" ironically, since it involves zero packing and absolutely no risk of throwing up on a mountain road.",
