    modelMonologue: "About six months ago I bought a proper set of bookshelves for my apartment, and it ended up costing almost double what I'd originally budgeted. I'd like to say I researched properly beforehand, but really I just typed \"wooden bookshelf\" into a shopping app and expected to spend around one million đồng for something decent.\n\nThe trigger was simply having too many books and nowhere sensible to put them. Since leaving my last job, I've had far more time to read, and stacks of books had started piling up on the floor, the windowsill, even part of my kitchen counter. After tripping over a small stack for the third time in a week, I finally decided to fix the problem properly instead of just complaining about the mess.\n\nThat's when the budget fell apart. Every shelf sturdy enough to hold dozens of hardcovers without sagging, with a design that actually suited my small living room, sat well above what I'd planned, while the cheaper options had reviews full of complaints about wobbling within months. After comparing options for almost two evenings, I gave in and bought a solid mid-range unit for close to two million, telling myself it counted as an investment in my own future reading corner rather than an impulsive splurge.\n\nHonestly, it was worth every extra đồng. My books finally have a proper home, and the corner near my window now genuinely looks like the reading nook I keep imagining for my future bookstore-café. It's a good reminder that spending a bit more upfront on something you use daily usually saves both money and frustration later.",
